{"id": "EUVD-2026-48928", "enisaUuid": "35a6eb95-80d8-39be-9f64-daa102f2add8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix change notify replay double-free\n\nA response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its\nresponse buffer. If SMB2_notify_init() fails before the next send, cleanup\nretains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.\n\nReset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:26", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5821f9dbb8b5b24391850a13418e633edd0fb003", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d684f4134998085702009b94c35c2003fc9e72d3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52af1975f0dfae990c5a0e85872cc41be0e88a68", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/901891513951bc8322ece754863909ea45af95c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/145f820dcbb2cced374f2532f8a61a44dce4a615"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hwgg-8wxq-m5c5", "CVE-2026-64384"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d8dec94-7d2a-372c-9339-44debcc11f4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "14fce211-9722-3cd4-bb2a-814f87e1f4e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1cd1aa97-31b5-3580-8ecd-8aff84ef8d70", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <52af1975f0dfae990c5a0e85872cc41be0e88a68"}, {"id": "1f6467c3-6a61-32ba-ba1d-a39ea5b617af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "3ffa258a-780d-3e84-9c28-3bee41a2ee87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <14